# Compline: the night office, in English, for a choir.
#
# Texts: the Book of Common Prayer (1662), its Coverdale psalter, the Authorized Version,
# and an 1851 translation of the hymn, all in the public domain. The antiphons
# and the hymn are sung to the plainsong melodies of their Latin originals, adapted.
#
# Make it with:  neuma book examples/compline/compline.book -o compline.pdf

page: a5
margins: 16mm 14mm 18mm 14mm
text-size: 11pt
staff-size: 6.5mm
initial: 1

title: Compline
rubric: The Reader begins.
text:
    Brethren, be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion,
    walketh about, seeking whom he may devour: whom resist stedfast in the faith.
text lines:
    V/ But thou, O Lord, have mercy upon us.
    R/ Thanks be to God.
text lines:
    V/ Our help is in the name of the Lord.
    R/ Who hath made heaven and earth.
rubric: Then all say the confession, the Lord’s Prayer and the absolution, as appointed.
text lines:
    V/ Turn us, O God our Saviour.
    R/ And let thine anger cease from us.
text lines:
    V/ O God, make speed to save us.
    R/ O Lord, make haste to help us.
text:
    Glory be to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Ghost;
    as it was in the beginning, is now, and ever shall be, world without end. Amen. Alleluia.

heading: The Psalms
rubric: The antiphon is begun by a cantor; the choir sings the psalms in alternate verses.
score: have-mercy.gabc
psalm tone=8.G gloria: psalm-4.txt
rubric: Psalm 91.
psalm tone=8.G gloria: psalm-91.txt
rubric: Psalm 134.
psalm tone=8.G gloria: psalm-134.txt
rubric: The antiphon is repeated.
score: have-mercy.gabc

heading: Hymn
score: before-the-ending.gabc
text center lines:
    From all ill dreams defend our eyes,
    From nightly fears and fantasies;
    Tread under foot our ghostly foe,
    That no pollution we may know.
text center lines:
    O Father, that we ask be done,
    Through Jesus Christ thine only Son,
    Who, with the Holy Ghost and thee,
    Doth live and reign eternally. Amen.

heading: Chapter
text:
    Thou, O Lord, art in the midst of us, and we are called by thy Name; leave us not,
    O Lord our God. <r>R/</r> Thanks be to God.
text lines:
    V/ Into thy hands, O Lord, I commend my spirit.
    R/ For thou hast redeemed me, O Lord, thou God of truth.
text lines:
    V/ Keep us, O Lord, as the apple of an eye.
    R/ Hide us under the shadow of thy wings.

heading: Nunc dimittis
score: preserve-us.gabc
psalm tone=3.a intone=every set=chant gloria: nunc-dimittis.txt
score: preserve-us.gabc

heading: The Prayers
rubric: All kneel.
text dropcap:
    Lighten our darkness, we beseech thee, O Lord; and by thy great mercy defend us from
    all perils and dangers of this night; for the love of thy only Son, our Saviour,
    Jesus Christ. Amen.
text lines:
    V/ The almighty and merciful Lord, the Father, the Son, and the Holy Ghost, bless and
    preserve us.
    R/ Amen.
